# Handoff: add the Creator Promo video template to the Nxeon app (per-partner renders)

Paste this whole file into your live Nxeon Claude Code session as the first message. It's self-contained. Attached: `nxeon-creator-promo-template.zip` (the complete, tested template project with every asset). Work on **staging first**, then production.

---

## 1. Goal

Let every Creator Partner generate their **own sponsor video** from the partner dashboard, with no human involved:

- the partner picks a **language** and **game** (optional handle) and clicks **Generate**;
- a background render produces a 50 s **1080p60 16:9 MP4**, optionally the **9:16** version and the **transparent overlay kit**, plus an end-frame PNG and a `HOW-TO-USE.txt`;
- the video shows **their real code** (`ReferralPartner.code`), their partner URL, their game, real prices and the program's real discount;
- admins can batch-queue renders for several partners (outreach use).

The template was built in a separate session. It is a standalone **HyperFrames** project (HTML → video, GSAP, rendered by headless Chrome + ffmpeg). The app never imports it. The app only builds a JSON **variables** object and shells out to the HyperFrames CLI inside a **separate render worker**.

## 2. Read first (two rules that change the design)

1. **Verify everything below against the live repo.** The code in this handoff was written from an Aug 31 snapshot of the app (Next.js 15 App Router, Prisma/Postgres, `Job` table + `worker/index.ts`, `ReferralPartner`, `lib/games.ts`, `lib/settings.ts`, `lib/auth.ts` → `requireUser()`, `components/ui/primitives.tsx`). The partner program has changed since (the Creator Partner Program has 50% first-order + 10% lifetime discounts and 40% commission). Model/field/helper names may differ. Treat the code as a **template to adapt**, not paste-ready.
2. **Do NOT render in the production worker or on the production web process.** `nxeon-worker` runs as root on the host that serves customers' VMs. A render saturates the CPU for minutes. That's why this uses its **own table (`PromoRender`) and its own systemd service** with CPU/memory caps, and why it deliberately does **not** reuse the `Job` table (the main worker claims *any* QUEUED job; adding a new `JobType` would put renders in its queue). Mirror its atomic-claim pattern instead.

Follow `CLAUDE.md`: update `docs/DOCUMENTATION.md` (§15 dated bullet + affected sections) and `ROADMAP.md` in the same commit, run `node scripts/publish-docs.mjs` after, `npm run build` must pass, never hardcode the domain (use `APP_URL`), never commit secrets, wallet amounts are integer cents.

## 3. What's in the zip (`nxeon-creator-promo-template.zip`)

Unzip to `/opt/nxeon/video-templates/creator-promo/` (staging: `/opt/nxeon-staging/video-templates/creator-promo/`). Do **not** put it under `app/`, `public/` or the Next build.

```
index.html                  16:9 composition (1920×1080, 50 s). Declares all variables (data-composition-variables)
compositions/vertical.html  9:16 composition (1080×1920)
compositions/overlay-sting.html / overlay-code.html / overlay-endcard.html   transparent overlays (ProRes 4444 alpha)
src/data.js                 beat timing table NX.T, games+covers NX.GAMES, translated overlay strings NX.STRINGS (en es tr hi tl)
src/lib.js  src/main.js     shared components, variable reading, the one paused GSAP timeline
src/scenes/s01–s13.js       one file per beat
src/promo.css  src/vertical.css  src/overlay.js
assets/fonts/               Geist, Geist Mono, Noto Sans Devanagari (OFL; licences included)
assets/brand/               logo-lockup.png, nx-mark.png, logo.png, icon.png, wallpaper.png
assets/covers/             38 portrait game covers (jpg/png/webp)
assets/flags/ icons/ mods/  region flags, 60 Nxeon icons, 9 mod icons cropped from the product
assets/vendor/gsap.min.js   GSAP 3.14.2, vendored so renders are offline/deterministic
creators.csv  tools/*.mjs   the CLI batch tools I used (kept for local/manual use; the app uses its own worker)
README.md BRIEF.md STORYBOARD.md frame.md storyboard.html   docs, design spec, beat plan
package.json                pins hyperframes@0.8.140
```

Not in the zip (too large; ask the owner if needed): the 15-minute screen recording the UI was rebuilt from and the finished MP4s.

## 4. Render contract

Render one video (Linux, from the template dir):

```bash
npx --yes hyperframes@0.8.140 render --quiet --strict-variables \
  --variables-file /tmp/vars.json -f 60 -q high -o /path/out.mp4            # 16:9
# 9:16: add   --composition compositions/vertical.html
# overlays:   --composition compositions/overlay-{sting|code|endcard}.html --format mov -f 60
```

A 16:9 final took ~2–2.5 min on the owner's laptop (AMD Ryzen AI 9, CPU-only; no GPU used). Expect **slower** on the i7-7700K, and slower again under a CPU cap, so measure on staging and set timeouts from the result. Always run `npx hyperframes check` after editing any template file (must be 0 errors).

### Variables (`--variables-file`, all optional except `code`)

| id | type | default | notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| `code` | string | `YOURCODE` | **A–Z 0–9 `_` `-`, up to 16 chars**; anything else is stripped by the template |
| `lang` | en/es/tr/hi/tl | `en` | translates overlays only; the recreated portal UI stays English on purpose |
| `game` | enum | `minecraft` | template keys: minecraft, minecraft-bedrock, valheim, rust, project-zomboid, palworld, factorio, the-forest, enshrouded, terraria |
| `creatorHandle` | string | `` | shows "with @handle" on the end card |
| `generic` | boolean | false | "USE MY CODE" + empty chip (for the overlay workflow) |
| `sponsoredTag` | boolean | true | small SPONSORED chip |
| `discountFirst` / `discountAfter` | number | 50 / 10 | shown as "−50%" badge and offer lines |
| `priceBefore` `priceAfter` `renewPrice` | string | `$4.99` `$2.49` `$7.18` | order-summary prices (Minecraft 2 GB from the recording) |
| `upgradePrice` `upgradeRenew` `tier8Price` | string | `$4.05` `$12.94` `$23.02` | upgrade beat |
| `playAddress` / `url` | string | derived | blank = `<code>.play.nxeon.cloud` / `nxeon.cloud/partner/<CODE>` |
| `gamesCount` | number | 46 | "N supported games" on the end card |

**The game swap changes only the game's name and cover** in the game-pick beat, order summary, dashboard header and end card. Settings, mods and the upgrade tiers stay Minecraft UI (they are real Minecraft screens). **Prices are not derived from the game**, so a Valheim video will show Minecraft's prices unless you pass real ones. See `promoPricing()` below. This is the #1 accuracy risk.

Frozen product facts in the template (from the 2026-10-08 portal recording): the three regions (Beauharnois CA, Singapore, Falkenstein DE), plan names "<Game> — 2/4/8 GB", the 7 deploy steps, the mod cards, the Resources/Settings screens. When the portal UI or plans change, update the scenes and **bump `PROMO_TEMPLATE_VERSION`** so cached renders regenerate.

## 5. Implementation plan (do in this order)

### Step 1: install the template and make it render on the server

1. Unzip as above. `cd` there. Check `node -v` (24 used so far; the app's Node is probably fine) and `ffmpeg -version`.
2. `npx hyperframes@0.8.140 doctor` and `npx hyperframes@0.8.140 browser` (see `--help`): install the Chrome/Chromium it needs and any system libs `doctor` reports. Run as the non-root render user (step 6).
3. Smoke test: write `/tmp/v.json` = `{"code":"TEST","lang":"en","game":"valheim"}` and render 16:9 with `-f 30 -q draft` first. Confirm it finishes with no network access to jsdelivr (GSAP is vendored) and note the wall time.

### Step 2: Prisma model (`prisma/schema.prisma`), then `npm run db:push`

```prisma
model PromoRender {
  id              String          @id @default(cuid())
  partnerId       String
  partner         ReferralPartner @relation(fields: [partnerId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  requestedById   String?         // User.id of the requester (partner or admin)
  status          String          @default("QUEUED") // QUEUED | RUNNING | DONE | FAILED | EXPIRED
  cacheKey        String          // sha256(templateVersion + vars + formats)
  templateVersion String
  vars            Json
  formats         String          @default("16x9") // comma list of: 16x9,9x16,overlays
  progress        Int             @default(0)
  step            String?
  error           String?
  attempts        Int             @default(0)
  outputDir       String?         // relative to PROMO_RENDER_DIR
  files           Json?           // [{ name, kind: "video"|"overlay"|"image"|"text", bytes }]
  createdAt       DateTime        @default(now())
  startedAt       DateTime?
  finishedAt      DateTime?

  @@index([status, createdAt])
  @@index([partnerId, createdAt])
  @@index([cacheKey])
}
// and on ReferralPartner:   promoRenders PromoRender[]
```

### Step 3: `lib/promo.ts` (server-only helpers)

```ts
import { createHash } from "node:crypto";
import { db } from "@/lib/db";
import { getSetting } from "@/lib/settings";
import { GAME_FAMILIES, GAME_DISPLAY, type GameFamily } from "@/lib/games";

export const PROMO_TEMPLATE_VERSION = "1.0.0"; // bump whenever video-templates/creator-promo changes visually
export const PROMO_LANGS = { en: "English", es: "Español", tr: "Türkçe", hi: "हिन्दी", tl: "Tagalog" } as const;
export type PromoLang = keyof typeof PROMO_LANGS;
export const PROMO_FORMATS = ["16x9", "9x16", "overlays"] as const;
export type PromoFormat = (typeof PROMO_FORMATS)[number];
const CODE_RE = /^[A-Z0-9_-]{2,16}$/;

/** App GameFamily → template game key. Families not listed are NOT offered (no cover/UI mapping in the template). */
export const PROMO_GAME_KEY: Partial<Record<GameFamily, string>> = {
  minecraft: "minecraft", bedrock: "minecraft-bedrock", valheim: "valheim", rust: "rust", palworld: "palworld",
  terraria: "terraria", projectzomboid: "project-zomboid", factorio: "factorio", theforest: "the-forest", enshrouded: "enshrouded",
};
export const promoGames = () => (Object.keys(PROMO_GAME_KEY) as GameFamily[]).map((f) => ({ family: f, name: GAME_DISPLAY[f].name }));

export type PromoPricing = { priceBefore: string; priceAfter: string; renewPrice: string; upgradePrice: string; upgradeRenew: string; tier8Price: string };

/**
 * MUST be implemented against the LIVE pricing for this game family. Return null if the family
 * doesn't have the three tiers (2/4/8 GB-equivalent) the upgrade beat shows → that game is hidden
 * from the generator rather than rendering wrong numbers.
 *   priceBefore  = first-month price of the entry tier;  priceAfter = priceBefore × (1 − discountFirstPct/100), 2 dp
 *   renewPrice   = entry tier's normal monthly price;     upgradeRenew = 2nd tier /mo;  tier8Price = 3rd tier /mo
 *   upgradePrice = illustrative prorated "due now" (the recording showed ~70% of the monthly difference)
 * Format like "$4.99" (currency symbol first, 2 decimals); wallet amounts elsewhere are integer cents, convert here.
 */
export async function promoPricing(family: GameFamily, discountFirstPct: number): Promise<PromoPricing | null> {
  throw new Error("TODO: implement from the live plan catalog");
}

export async function buildPromoVars(partner: { code: string }, o: { lang: PromoLang; family: GameFamily; handle?: string }) {
  const code = partner.code.toUpperCase();
  if (!CODE_RE.test(code)) throw new Error("This partner code can't be used in a video (A–Z, 0–9, _ or -, 2–16 characters).");
  const game = PROMO_GAME_KEY[o.family];
  if (!game) throw new Error("That game isn't available for promo videos yet.");
  // TODO: read the REAL program values (50% first order, 10% lifetime) from wherever the Creator Partner Program stores them.
  const d1 = Number(await getSetting("partner_first_order_discount_pct", "50"));
  const d2 = Number(await getSetting("partner_lifetime_discount_pct", "10"));
  const pricing = await promoPricing(o.family, d1);
  if (!pricing) throw new Error("Pricing for this game isn't available.");
  const host = new URL(process.env.APP_URL ?? "https://nxeon.cloud").host;
  return {
    code, lang: o.lang, game, discountFirst: d1, discountAfter: d2, ...pricing,
    url: `${host}/partner/${code}`, creatorHandle: (o.handle ?? "").replace(/^@/, "").slice(0, 30),
    gamesCount: GAME_FAMILIES.length, // or the live "supported games" number the marketing site uses
  };
}

const sorted = (o: any): any => Array.isArray(o) ? o.map(sorted) : o && typeof o === "object" ? Object.fromEntries(Object.keys(o).sort().map((k) => [k, sorted(o[k])])) : o;
const MAX_PER_DAY = Number(process.env.PROMO_MAX_PER_DAY ?? 6);

/** Idempotent: identical requests reuse the existing render; otherwise rate-limited insert. */
export async function requestPromo(partnerId: string, requestedById: string | null, vars: Record<string, unknown>, formats: PromoFormat[], opts?: { bypassLimit?: boolean }) {
  const fmts = [...new Set(formats)].sort();
  const cacheKey = createHash("sha256").update(JSON.stringify(sorted({ v: PROMO_TEMPLATE_VERSION, vars, fmts }))).digest("hex");
  const existing = await db.promoRender.findFirst({ where: { partnerId, cacheKey, status: { in: ["QUEUED", "RUNNING", "DONE"] } }, orderBy: { createdAt: "desc" } });
  if (existing) return existing;
  if (!opts?.bypassLimit) {
    const n = await db.promoRender.count({ where: { partnerId, createdAt: { gte: new Date(Date.now() - 86_400_000) } } });
    if (n >= MAX_PER_DAY) throw new Error("Daily video limit reached. Try again tomorrow.");
  }
  return db.promoRender.create({ data: { partnerId, requestedById, cacheKey, templateVersion: PROMO_TEMPLATE_VERSION, vars: vars as any, formats: fmts.join(",") } });
}
```

Port `note()` from the template's `tools/creator-kit.mjs` (it generates `HOW-TO-USE.txt` from code/url/discounts) into `lib/promo-howto.ts` as a pure function; the worker calls it.

### Step 4: API routes

`app/api/partner/*` is the **Kodely server-to-server API (X-Api-Key)**. Don't mix. Use `app/api/promo/*` with the normal session cookie.

- `app/api/promo/route.ts`: `GET` returns the signed-in partner's last 10 renders (id, status, progress, step, error, formats, files, createdAt) and the offered games/langs; `POST {lang, family, handle?, formats[]}` → `requireUser()` → `partner = await db.referralPartner.findUnique({ where: { userId: user.id } })` (403 if none or `status !== "ACTIVE"`) → validate `lang`/`family`/`formats` against the allow-lists → `buildPromoVars` → `requestPromo` → return the row. Wrap errors as 400 with the message.
- `app/api/promo/[id]/file/[name]/route.ts` (Next 15: `params` is a Promise):

```ts
import { createReadStream } from "node:fs"; import { stat } from "node:fs/promises"; import { join } from "node:path"; import { Readable } from "node:stream";
const ROOT = process.env.PROMO_RENDER_DIR ?? "/var/lib/nxeon/promo-renders";
export async function GET(_: Request, { params }: { params: Promise<{ id: string; name: string }> }) {
  const { id, name } = await params;
  const user = await requireUser();
  const r = await db.promoRender.findUnique({ where: { id }, include: { partner: true } });
  const allowed = !!r && (r.partner.userId === user.id /* || user is admin: use the app's existing admin check, and never while impersonating */);
  const f = allowed && r!.status === "DONE" ? (r!.files as any[] | null)?.find((x) => x.name === name) : null; // name must be in the recorded list: no path building from user input
  if (!f) return new Response("Not found", { status: 404 });
  const p = join(ROOT, r!.outputDir!, f.name);
  const s = await stat(p).catch(() => null);
  if (!s) return new Response("Expired", { status: 410 });
  const type = f.name.endsWith(".mp4") ? "video/mp4" : f.name.endsWith(".mov") ? "video/quicktime" : f.name.endsWith(".png") ? "image/png" : "text/plain; charset=utf-8";
  return new Response(Readable.toWeb(createReadStream(p)) as any, { headers: { "content-type": type, "content-length": String(s.size), "content-disposition": `attachment; filename="${f.name}"`, "cache-control": "private, no-store" } });
}
```

### Step 5: partner dashboard card

Add a "Promo video" card to `app/dashboard/partner/page.tsx` (below the existing summary) using the existing design system (`card`, `Badge`, `timeAgo` from `components/ui/primitives`, navy/glass styling; no new libs). A client component `components/customer/PromoVideoCard.tsx`:

- selects: language (`PROMO_LANGS`), game (`promoGames()`), optional handle input (max 30), checkboxes **16:9** (default on), **9:16**, **Overlay kit (large files)**; a **Generate video** button → `POST /api/promo`;
- list of recent renders: status badge, a progress bar from `progress`/`step` while QUEUED/RUNNING (poll `GET /api/promo` every 3 s only while something is active), and on DONE a file list with download links (`/api/promo/{id}/file/{name}`), the end-frame PNG thumbnail link and the `HOW-TO-USE.txt`;
- copy under the button: "Takes a few minutes. Tick YouTube's 'Includes paid promotion' box. Have a native speaker check translated overlays before publishing."

### Step 6: the render worker (separate process)

`worker-render/index.ts`, started by its own service. Mirrors `worker/index.ts`'s loop and atomic claim; imports `db` from `../lib/db`.

```ts
import { spawn } from "node:child_process";
import { mkdir, writeFile, rm, rename, stat, readdir } from "node:fs/promises";
import { join } from "node:path";
import { db } from "../lib/db";
import { howToUse } from "../lib/promo-howto";

const TPL = process.env.PROMO_TEMPLATE_DIR ?? "/opt/nxeon/video-templates/creator-promo";
const ROOT = process.env.PROMO_RENDER_DIR ?? "/var/lib/nxeon/promo-renders";
const HF = "hyperframes@0.8.140";
const POLL_MS = 5000, TIMEOUT_MS = Number(process.env.PROMO_TIMEOUT_MS ?? 30 * 60_000);
const RETENTION_DAYS = Number(process.env.PROMO_RETENTION_DAYS ?? 14);

function run(cmd: string, args: string[], cwd: string): Promise<void> {            // NO shell, args array only
  return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
    const p = spawn(cmd, args, { cwd, stdio: ["ignore", "pipe", "pipe"] });
    let tail = ""; const keep = (b: Buffer) => { tail = (tail + b.toString()).slice(-4000); };
    p.stdout.on("data", keep); p.stderr.on("data", keep);
    const t = setTimeout(() => p.kill("SIGKILL"), TIMEOUT_MS);
    p.on("error", reject);
    p.on("close", (c) => { clearTimeout(t); c === 0 ? resolve() : reject(new Error(`${cmd} exited ${c}: ${tail.slice(-600)}`)); });
  });
}
const hf = (vf: string, out: string, extra: string[]) =>
  ["--yes", HF, "render", "--quiet", "--strict-variables", "--variables-file", vf, "-w", process.env.PROMO_WORKERS ?? "2", "-o", out, ...extra];

async function render(r: { id: string; partnerId: string; vars: any; formats: string }) {
  const code: string = r.vars.code, lang: string = r.vars.lang;
  const rel = `${r.partnerId}/${r.id}`, tmp = join(ROOT, ".tmp", r.id), final = join(ROOT, rel);
  await rm(tmp, { recursive: true, force: true }); await mkdir(tmp, { recursive: true });
  const vf = join(tmp, "vars.json"); await writeFile(vf, JSON.stringify(r.vars));
  const want = r.formats.split(",");
  const tasks: { label: string; out: string; args: string[] }[] = [];
  if (want.includes("16x9")) tasks.push({ label: "16:9 video", out: `nxeon-promo_${code}_${lang}_16x9.mp4`, args: ["-f", "60", "-q", "high"] });
  if (want.includes("9x16")) tasks.push({ label: "9:16 video", out: `nxeon-promo_${code}_${lang}_9x16.mp4`, args: ["-f", "60", "-q", "high", "--composition", "compositions/vertical.html"] });
  if (want.includes("overlays")) for (const k of ["sting", "code", "endcard"]) tasks.push({ label: `overlay: ${k}`, out: `nxeon-overlay_${k}_${code}.mov`, args: ["--format", "mov", "-f", "60", "--composition", `compositions/overlay-${k}.html`] });
  const files: { name: string; kind: string; bytes: number }[] = [];
  for (const [i, t] of tasks.entries()) {
    await db.promoRender.update({ where: { id: r.id }, data: { step: `Rendering ${t.label}`, progress: Math.round((i / (tasks.length + 1)) * 100) } });
    await run("npx", hf(vf, join(tmp, t.out), t.args), TPL);
    files.push({ name: t.out, kind: t.out.endsWith(".mov") ? "overlay" : "video", bytes: (await stat(join(tmp, t.out))).size });
    if (t.out.endsWith(".mp4")) {                                                           // end-frame PNG for thumbnails
      const png = t.out.replace(/\.mp4$/, "_endframe.png");
      await run("ffmpeg", ["-v", "error", "-y", "-sseof", "-0.1", "-i", join(tmp, t.out), "-frames:v", "1", join(tmp, png)], tmp);
      files.push({ name: png, kind: "image", bytes: (await stat(join(tmp, png))).size });
    }
  }
  await writeFile(join(tmp, "HOW-TO-USE.txt"), howToUse(r.vars, files.map((f) => f.name)));
  files.push({ name: "HOW-TO-USE.txt", kind: "text", bytes: (await stat(join(tmp, "HOW-TO-USE.txt"))).size });
  await rm(join(tmp, "vars.json"));
  await mkdir(join(ROOT, r.partnerId), { recursive: true }); await rm(final, { recursive: true, force: true }); await rename(tmp, final);
  return { rel, files };
}

async function main() {
  await mkdir(ROOT, { recursive: true });
  await db.promoRender.updateMany({ where: { status: "RUNNING" }, data: { status: "QUEUED" } });   // single worker: anything RUNNING at boot is stale
  let lastSweep = 0;
  for (;;) {
    try {
      if (Date.now() - lastSweep > 3_600_000) { lastSweep = Date.now(); await sweepExpired(); }
      const c = await db.promoRender.findFirst({ where: { status: "QUEUED" }, orderBy: { createdAt: "asc" } });
      if (!c) { await new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, POLL_MS)); continue; }
      const claim = await db.promoRender.updateMany({ where: { id: c.id, status: "QUEUED" }, data: { status: "RUNNING", attempts: { increment: 1 }, startedAt: new Date(), error: null } });
      if (claim.count !== 1) continue;
      try {
        const { rel, files } = await render(c as any);
        await db.promoRender.update({ where: { id: c.id }, data: { status: "DONE", progress: 100, step: "Done", outputDir: rel, files, finishedAt: new Date() } });
      } catch (e: any) {
        const retry = c.attempts + 1 < 2;
        await db.promoRender.update({ where: { id: c.id }, data: { status: retry ? "QUEUED" : "FAILED", error: String(e?.message ?? e).slice(0, 1500), step: null } });
      }
    } catch (e) { console.error("[render-worker]", e); await new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, POLL_MS)); }
  }
}
async function sweepExpired() {          // delete files of DONE renders older than RETENTION_DAYS, keep the row as EXPIRED
  const old = await db.promoRender.findMany({ where: { status: "DONE", finishedAt: { lt: new Date(Date.now() - RETENTION_DAYS * 86_400_000) } } });
  for (const r of old) { if (r.outputDir) await rm(join(ROOT, r.outputDir), { recursive: true, force: true }); await db.promoRender.update({ where: { id: r.id }, data: { status: "EXPIRED", files: null } }); }
}
main();
```

