**The game swap changes only the game's name and cover** in the game-pick beat, order summary, dashboard header and end card. Settings, mods and the upgrade tiers stay Minecraft UI (they are real Minecraft screens). **Prices are not derived from the game**, so a Valheim video will show Minecraft's prices unless you pass real ones. See `promoPricing()` below. This is the #1 accuracy risk.

Frozen product facts in the template (from the 2026-10-08 portal recording): the three regions (Beauharnois CA, Singapore, Falkenstein DE), plan names "<Game> — 2/4/8 GB", the 7 deploy steps, the mod cards, the Resources/Settings screens. When the portal UI or plans change, update the scenes and **bump `PROMO_TEMPLATE_VERSION`** so cached renders regenerate.

## 5. Implementation plan (do in this order)

### Step 1: install the template and make it render on the server

